      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "The determinant of a matrix raised to a power is equal to the determinant of the matrix raised to that power. Additionally, the determinant of a matrix is equal to the determinant of its transpose. Therefore,\n\\begin{align*}\n\\det (\\mathbf{M}^4) &= \\det (\\mathbf{M} \\cdot \\mathbf{M} \\cdot \\mathbf{M} \\cdot \\mathbf{M}) \\\\\n&= \\det (\\mathbf{M} \\cdot \\mathbf{M}) \\cdot \\det (\\mathbf{M})^3 \\\\\n&= \\det (\\mathbf{M})^4 \\\\\n&= (-2)^4 \\\\\n&= \\boxed{16}.\n\\end{align*}. The answer is 16",
